                <pb facs="0984" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg868"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5482.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-13T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1912—12
                        noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rebels now control entire coast of Guerrero, most of Michoacán and the State of
                    Mexico, and are increasing in northern Chiapas.</p>
                <p>Many political arrests and domiciliary visits by the police are being made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
